msgctxt "a_seedphrase_lets_you_recover_your_account"
msgid "A seedphrase lets you recover your account if you lose access."
msgstr "Uma frase-semente permite recuperar sua conta se você perder o acesso."

msgctxt "a_seedphrase_lets_you_recover_your_account_2"
msgid "A seedphrase lets you recover your account if you lose access. Store it safely."
msgstr "Uma frase-semente permite recuperar sua conta se você perder o acesso. Guarde-a em um local seguro."

#. Settings: heading of the about section.
msgctxt "about"
msgid "About"
msgstr "Sobre"

#. Instructions for accessing the authentication code.
#. Use the {link}...{/link} markers to wrap the "ur.io" portion, which should be rendered as a clickable link.
#. Example usage:
#.   - Web: Replace {link} with <a href="https://ur.io" target="_blank"> and {/link} with </a>
#.   - SwiftUI: Use AttributedString parsing to detect {link}...{/link} and apply .link attribute to the range
#.   - Jetpack Compose: Use AnnotatedString with an annotation for the {link}...{/link} range, and handle clicks accordingly
#. 
msgctxt "access_auth_code_instructions"
msgid "To Access your Auth Code, create an account and sign in to {link}ur.io{/link}. Head over to Account -> Settings -> Create/Copy Auth code -> Paste -> UR In!"
msgstr "Para acessar seu código de autenticação, crie uma conta e faça login em {link}ur.io{/link}. Vá para Conta -> Configurações -> Criar/Copiar código de autenticação -> Colar -> Pronto!"

#. Account Screen
msgctxt "account"
msgid "Account"
msgstr "Conta"

#. The account's email or phone, marked as not yet verified. The argument is the email or phone number.
msgctxt "account_auth_unverified"
msgid "{} (unverified)"
msgstr "{} (não verificado)"

#. The account's email or phone, marked as verified. The argument is the email or phone number.
msgctxt "account_auth_verified"
msgid "{} (verified)"
msgstr "{} (verificado)"

#. Shown when a purchase is refused before contacting the store because the account is not ready: on apple the networkId is missing or unparseable (Shared/ViewModels/AppStoreSubscriptionManager.swift), on android the active network space has no api yet (the Stripe sheet and pay page purchasers). The purchase could never be credited to anyone. This used to be a silent no-op.
msgctxt "account_isn_t_ready_for_purchases"
msgid "Your account isn't ready for purchases. Please restart the app and try again."
msgstr "Sua conta ainda não está pronta para compras. Reinicie o app e tente novamente."

#. Accessibility label of the row of rings, one per extender carrying a live connection.
msgctxt "active_extenders"
msgid "Active extenders"
msgstr "Extensores ativos"

#. A heading for the list of current block actions.
msgctxt "activity"
msgid "Activity"
msgstr "Atividade"

#. dns settings
msgctxt "add"
msgid "Add"
msgstr "Adicionar"

#. Split rules: the button (and its icon's accessibility label) that adds the typed host to the rule.
msgctxt "add_a_rule"
msgid "Add a rule"
msgstr "Adicionar uma regra"

#. A title for the screen that lets the user add a new sign-in method.
msgctxt "add_a_sign_in_method"
msgid "Add a sign-in method"
msgstr "Adicionar um método de login"

#. Split rules screen on macOS, Apps section: the row (and the title of the sheet it opens) that adds an app from /Applications to the apps that bypass the VPN.
msgctxt "add_an_app"
msgid "Add an app"
msgstr "Adicionar um app"

#. Call to action
msgctxt "add_blocked_location"
msgid "Add blocked location"
msgstr "Adicionar localização bloqueada"

#. Points leaderboard: button that opens the emoji tag editor when no tag is set yet.
msgctxt "add_emoji"
msgid "Add emoji"
msgstr "Adicionar emoji"

#. Call to action on a split-rule activity row blocked by URnetwork safety rules: create a local split rule for its hosts.
msgctxt "add_local_split_rule"
msgid "Route locally"
msgstr "Rotear localmente"

#. Call to action
msgctxt "add_referral_code"
msgid "Add referral code"
msgstr "Adicionar código de indicação"

msgctxt "add_sign_in_method"
msgid "Add sign-in method"
msgstr "Adicionar método de login"

#. Button text for adding a sign-in method.
msgctxt "add_sign_in_method_2"
msgid "Add Sign-In Method"
msgstr "Adicionar método de login"

#. State when the gas key has no TAO.
msgctxt "add_tao_for_gas"
msgid "Add TAO for gas"
msgstr "Adicione TAO para o gás"

#. A description of the user's ability to provide bandwidth.
msgctxt "adjust_setting_always_fill_data_faster"
msgid "Providing is off by default. Choose when your device provides below."
msgstr "Você pode ajustar a configuração para \"Sempre\" para preencher os dados gratuitos mais rápido."

#. Connection inspector: label of the action id row.
msgctxt "adv_action_id"
msgid "Action id"
msgstr "ID da ação"

#. Connection inspector: label of the addresses row.
msgctxt "adv_addresses"
msgid "Addresses"
msgstr "Endereços"

#. Settings: switch that turns advanced mode on.
msgctxt "adv_advanced_mode"
msgid "Advanced mode"
msgstr "Modo avançado"

#. Settings: explanation under the advanced mode switch.
msgctxt "adv_advanced_mode_note"
msgid "Show raw values, identifiers, the connection inspector and the reliability tuning surface across the app."
msgstr "Mostra valores brutos, identificadores, o inspetor de conexão e os ajustes de confiabilidade em todo o app."

#. Connect page, Advanced Mode, the connection inspector and an Activity row's menu: the button that allows the connection's host. It adds an allowing rule for a host that was blocked, or removes the rule blocking it while one is in force, so the label always names what the press leaves behind.
msgctxt "adv_allow_host"
msgid "Allow this host"
msgstr "Permitir este host"

#. Connect page, Advanced Mode, the connection inspector and an Activity row's menu: the button that keeps the connection's host inside the VPN tunnel. It adds a rule for a host that bypassed the tunnel, or removes the bypass rule while one is in force.
msgctxt "adv_always_tunnel"
msgid "Always tunnel"
msgstr "Sempre pelo túnel"

#. Windows split tunnel, App split rules sheet: the line at the top that says what including and excluding an app do.
msgctxt "adv_app_rules_note"
msgid "Including an app sends its traffic through the VPN, while excluding it keeps that app's traffic off the VPN."
msgstr "Incluir um app envia o tráfego dele pela VPN, enquanto excluí-lo mantém o tráfego desse app fora da VPN."

#. Network page, selected provider pane: note under the Name row while Best available provider is selected, saying what best available means.
msgctxt "adv_best_available_note"
msgid "URnetwork picks the fastest healthy providers for you, with no location constraint, and re-picks as the network changes."
msgstr "O URnetwork escolhe para você os provedores operacionais mais rápidos, sem restrição de localização, e escolhe de novo conforme a rede muda."

#. Connect page, Advanced Mode, the connection inspector and an Activity row's menu: the button that blocks the connection's host. It adds a blocking rule, or removes the rule allowing the host while one is in force, so the label always names what the press leaves behind.
msgctxt "adv_block_host"
msgid "Block this host"
msgstr "Bloquear este host"

#. Windows sign-in screen, browser sign-in sheet: the text above the auth code field that says how the sheet works. ur.io, Google and Apple are names. The Google or Apple sessions are the sign-ins the browser already holds. 'Account → Create auth code' is the way to the Create auth code button on a signed-in device: use this language's labels of Account (account) and Create auth code (site_app_create_auth_code); right-to-left languages point the arrow the other way.
msgctxt "adv_browser_sign_in_body"
msgid "Sign in at ur.io in your browser — your password manager and existing Google or Apple sessions work there. Then paste a one-time auth code from any signed-in device (Account → Create auth code)."
msgstr "Entre no ur.io pelo navegador — seu gerenciador de senhas e as sessões do Google ou da Apple já abertas funcionam lá. Depois, cole um código de autenticação de uso único de qualquer dispositivo conectado (Conta → Criar código de autenticação)."

#. Windows sign-in screen: the title of the sheet for signing in through the browser at ur.io with a one-time auth code.
msgctxt "adv_browser_sign_in_title"
msgid "Browser sign-in"
msgstr "Login pelo navegador"

#. Connect page, Advanced Mode, the connection inspector and an Activity row's menu: the button that sends the connection's host directly from this device, outside the VPN. It adds a split rule, or removes the rule keeping the host in the tunnel while one is in force.
msgctxt "adv_bypass_tunnel"
msgid "Bypass the tunnel"
msgstr "Contornar o túnel"

#. Connection inspector: label of the total bytes row.
msgctxt "adv_bytes_total"
msgid "Bytes (total)"
msgstr "Bytes (total)"

#. Connection inspector: button that clears the selected connection.
msgctxt "adv_clear_selection"
msgid "Clear selection"
msgstr "Limpar seleção"

#. Windows split tunnel, App split rules sheet: the header over the apps that already have a rule (included or excluded). The header of the other list is Apps.
msgctxt "adv_configured"
msgid "Configured"
msgstr "Configurados"

#. Connect page, Activity pane, grouped by host: how many connections (routing decisions) one host's row stands for, at the start of the row's figures and in its accessible name. The argument is the number of connections.
msgctxt "adv_connection_count"
msgid "{} connection"
msgid_plural "{} connections"
msgstr[0] "{} conexão"
msgstr[1] "{} conexões"

#. Connect page, Advanced Mode, the connection inspector and an Activity row's menu: the button that copies the connection's details (host, addresses, verdict, reason, totals) to the clipboard.
msgctxt "adv_copy_details"
msgid "Copy details"
msgstr "Copiar detalhes"

#. Connect page, Advanced Mode, the connection inspector and an Activity row's menu: the confirmation after Copy details put the connection's details on the clipboard.
msgctxt "adv_details_copied"
msgid "Connection details copied"
msgstr "Detalhes da conexão copiados"

#. Windows Earnings page, ledger header: the tooltip and screen reader name of the icon-only More button, which holds the earnings actions when the window is too narrow to show them.
msgctxt "adv_earnings_actions"
msgid "Earnings actions"
msgstr "Ações de ganhos"

#. Connection inspector: label of the exit dial failures row.
msgctxt "adv_exit_dial_failures"
msgid "Dial failures"
msgstr "Falhas de discagem"

#. Connection inspector: label of the flows to the selected destination.
msgctxt "adv_exit_flows"
msgid "Flows to this destination"
msgstr "Fluxos para este destino"

#. Connection inspector: label of the exit flows row.
msgctxt "adv_exit_flows_total"
msgid "Exit flows"
msgstr "Fluxos de saída"

#. Connection inspector: exit state, OK.
msgctxt "adv_exit_ok"
msgid "OK"
msgstr "OK"

#. Connection inspector: exit state, proven.
msgctxt "adv_exit_proven"
msgid "Proven"
msgstr "Comprovada"

#. Connection inspector: exit state, quarantined.
msgctxt "adv_exit_quarantined"
msgid "Quarantined"
msgstr "Em quarentena"

#. Connection inspector: label of the exit state row.
msgctxt "adv_exit_state"
msgid "Exit state"
msgstr "Estado da saída"

#. Connection inspector: label of the exit tier row.
msgctxt "adv_exit_tier"
msgid "Exit tier"
msgstr "Nível da saída"

#. Connection inspector: exit state, warning.
msgctxt "adv_exit_warning"
msgid "Warning"
msgstr "Aviso"

#. Connection inspector: label of the warning cause row.
msgctxt "adv_exit_warning_cause"
msgid "Warning cause"
msgstr "Causa do aviso"

#. Connection inspector: heading of the exits section.
msgctxt "adv_exits"
msgid "Exits"
msgstr "Saídas"

#. Connect page, Activity pane: the first choice of the verdict filter above the list of connections (routing decisions). Shows every connection, whatever its verdict. Short: it shares one row with Blocked, Tunnelled and Bypassed.
msgctxt "adv_filter_all"
msgid "All"
msgstr "Todas"

#. Connect page, Activity pane: the verdict filter choice that shows only the connections that bypassed the tunnel (allowed, but sent directly from this device outside the VPN, for example by a split rule, so not protected). Short: it shares one row with All, Blocked and Tunnelled.
msgctxt "adv_filter_bypassed"
msgid "Bypassed"
msgstr "Fora do túnel"

#. Connect page, Activity pane: the verdict filter choice that shows only the connections sent through the URnetwork tunnel (allowed and protected). Short: it shares one row with All, Blocked and Bypassed.
msgctxt "adv_filter_tunnelled"
msgid "Tunnelled"
msgstr "Pelo túnel"

#. Connect page, Activity pane: label of the switch beside the search field that folds the list of connections into one row per host (with the count, the summed traffic and the latest decision). Clicking a host's row turns the switch off and searches for that host.
msgctxt "adv_group_by_host"
msgid "Group by host"
msgstr "Agrupar por host"

#. Connection inspector: label of the host row.
msgctxt "adv_host"
msgid "Host"
msgstr "Host"

#. Connect page, Advanced Mode, the connection inspector and an Activity row's menu: the confirmation after a press added a rule allowing the connection's host from now on.
msgctxt "adv_host_allowed"
msgid "This host will be allowed"
msgstr "Este host será permitido"

#. Connect page, Advanced Mode, the connection inspector and an Activity row's menu: the confirmation after a press added a rule blocking the connection's host from now on.
msgctxt "adv_host_blocked"
msgid "This host will be blocked"
msgstr "Este host será bloqueado"

#. Connect page, Advanced Mode, the connection inspector and an Activity row's menu: the confirmation after a press added a split rule sending the connection's host outside the VPN tunnel from now on.
msgctxt "adv_host_bypassed"
msgid "This host will bypass the tunnel"
msgstr "Este host vai contornar o túnel"

#. Connect page, Advanced Mode, the connection inspector and an Activity row's menu: the confirmation after a press added a rule keeping the connection's host inside the VPN tunnel from now on.
msgctxt "adv_host_tunnelled"
msgid "This host will use the tunnel"
msgstr "Este host vai usar o túnel"

#. Connection inspector: heading of the inspector pane.
msgctxt "adv_inspector"
msgid "Inspector"
msgstr "Inspetor"

#. Kill switch: status while the change is being applied.
msgctxt "adv_kill_switch_applying"
msgid "Applying…"
msgstr "Aplicando…"

#. Kill switch: how to restore normal access while the block is armed.
msgctxt "adv_kill_switch_armed_way_out"
msgid "Turn the kill switch off to restore normal access without connecting."
msgstr "Desligue o Kill switch para restaurar o acesso normal sem conectar."

#. Settings, kill switch: Disconnect always restores the internet; the switch only covers drops the user did not ask for.
msgctxt "adv_kill_switch_deliberate"
msgid "Pressing Disconnect always restores your internet straight away. The kill switch only applies to drops you did not ask for - a tunnel that stops carrying traffic, a network change, or the URnetwork service stopping."
msgstr "Tocar em Desconectar sempre restaura a internet na hora. O Kill switch só vale para quedas que você não pediu - um túnel que para de transportar tráfego, uma troca de rede ou a parada do serviço URnetwork."

#. Settings, kill switch: what may leave the device while the switch is on, and the name-lookup window during a connection attempt.
msgctxt "adv_kill_switch_dns_window"
msgid "While it is on and nothing is connecting, nothing leaves this device - name lookups included. During a connection attempt, name lookups from any app on this device can leave in the clear so URnetwork can reach its servers; everything else stays blocked."
msgstr "Enquanto está ligado e nada está conectando, nada sai deste dispositivo - nem as consultas de nomes. Durante uma tentativa de conexão, as consultas de nomes de qualquer app deste dispositivo podem sair sem criptografia para que a URnetwork alcance seus servidores; todo o resto continua bloqueado."

#. Settings: explanation under the kill switch switch.
msgctxt "adv_kill_switch_note"
msgid "If the tunnel drops unexpectedly, block this device's traffic instead of letting it out unprotected."
msgstr "Se o túnel cair de forma inesperada, bloqueia o tráfego deste dispositivo em vez de deixá-lo sair sem proteção."

#. Kill switch: how to remove a block that is still in place when the device cannot reach the network; {command} is the shell command.
msgctxt "adv_kill_switch_recovery"
msgid "If this device cannot reach the network, a block installed earlier may still be in place; remove it with: {}"
msgstr "Se este dispositivo não consegue acessar a rede, um bloqueio instalado antes pode ainda estar em vigor; remova-o com: {}"

#. Kill switch status: in force and armed, only local traffic leaves until connected.
msgctxt "adv_kill_switch_state_armed"
msgid "In force: nothing but local network traffic leaves this device until you connect."
msgstr "Em vigor: nada além do tráfego da rede local sai deste dispositivo até você conectar."

#. Kill switch status: in force while connected, traffic is blocked if the tunnel drops.
msgctxt "adv_kill_switch_state_connected"
msgid "In force: if the tunnel drops, this device's traffic is blocked instead of going out unprotected."
msgstr "Em vigor: se o túnel cair, o tráfego deste dispositivo é bloqueado em vez de sair sem proteção."

#. Kill switch status: the system service could not install the block.
msgctxt "adv_kill_switch_state_failed"
msgid "The URnetwork system service could not install the kill switch, so your traffic is NOT being blocked."
msgstr "O serviço do sistema URnetwork não conseguiu instalar o Kill switch, então o tráfego não está sendo bloqueado."

#. Kill switch status: not in force, traffic is not blocked.
msgctxt "adv_kill_switch_state_not_in_force"
msgid "The kill switch is NOT in force: your traffic is not being blocked."
msgstr "O Kill switch NÃO está em vigor: seu tráfego não está sendo bloqueado."

#. Kill switch status: nothing is blocked yet, takes effect on connect.
msgctxt "adv_kill_switch_state_pending"
msgid "Nothing is blocked yet — this takes effect the moment you connect."
msgstr "Nada está bloqueado ainda — passa a valer no momento em que você conectar."

#. Kill switch status: the switch is off but the service still has a block installed, so traffic is blocked.
msgctxt "adv_kill_switch_state_still_installed"
msgid "The kill switch is off, but the URnetwork system service still has a block installed, so this device's traffic is being blocked."
msgstr "O Kill switch está desligado, mas o serviço do sistema URnetwork ainda tem um bloqueio instalado, então o tráfego deste dispositivo está sendo bloqueado."

#. Kill switch status: cannot be checked right now.
msgctxt "adv_kill_switch_state_unknown"
msgid "Whether the kill switch is in force cannot be checked right now."
msgstr "Não é possível verificar agora se o Kill switch está em vigor."

#. Kill switch: how to clear a block the service still has installed; {command} is the shell command to use if toggling does not work.
msgctxt "adv_kill_switch_still_installed_fix"
msgid "Turning the kill switch on and then off again asks the service to clear it; if that does not work, remove it with: {}"
msgstr "Ligar e desligar de novo o Kill switch pede ao serviço que o remova; se isso não funcionar, remova-o com: {}"

#. Connection inspector: label of the last routing decision row.
msgctxt "adv_last_decision"
msgid "Last decision"
msgstr "Última decisão"

#. Connection inspector: label of the matched rule row.
msgctxt "adv_matched"
msgid "Matched"
msgstr "Correspondência"

#. Windows status strip (Advanced Mode), Session value: a session that talks to the service over RPC without a tunnel. Lowercase, a short status value.
msgctxt "adv_mode_rpc_only"
msgid "rpc-only"
msgstr "só RPC"

#. Windows and Linux status strip (Advanced Mode), Session value: a full tunnel session. Lowercase, a short status value.
msgctxt "adv_mode_tunnel"
msgid "tunnel"
msgstr "túnel"

#. Connection inspector: placeholder dash for a value that is not available.
msgctxt "adv_na"
msgid "—"
msgstr "—"

#. Split rules sheet: the line in the Activity list when the search matches none of the connections it holds.
msgctxt "adv_no_activity_matches"
msgid "No activity matches this search."
msgstr "Nenhuma atividade corresponde a esta busca."

#. Connection inspector: shown when no connection is selected.
msgctxt "adv_no_selection"
msgid "No connection selected"
msgstr "Nenhuma conexão selecionada"

#. Connection inspector: value shown when a field has nothing.
msgctxt "adv_none"
msgid "none"
msgstr "nenhum"

#. Connect page, Advanced Mode, the connection inspector: the end of the Reason value's name for screen readers when a rule decided the connection, because pressing the value opens the Split rules sheet. Lowercase: it follows a comma.
msgctxt "adv_open_split_rules"
msgid "open split rules"
msgstr "abrir regras de divisão"

#. Windows sign-in screen, browser sign-in sheet: the button that opens ur.io in the browser and leaves the sheet open. ur.io is a domain name. Keep it short: three buttons share the sheet's bar.
msgctxt "adv_open_ur_io"
msgid "Open ur.io"
msgstr "Abrir ur.io"

#. Connection inspector: label of the override id row.
msgctxt "adv_override_id"
msgid "Override"
msgstr "Substituição"

#. Connection inspector: label of the total packets row.
msgctxt "adv_packets_total"
msgid "Packets (total)"
msgstr "Pacotes (total)"

#. Network page, selected provider pane: note under the best available explanation, saying how to connect to a chosen location instead.
msgctxt "adv_pick_location_note"
msgid "Pick a country, region, city or device in the list to connect there instead."
msgstr "Escolha um país, região, cidade ou dispositivo na lista para se conectar a ele."

#. Connection inspector: label of the probe age row.
msgctxt "adv_probe_age"
msgid "Probe age"
msgstr "Idade da sonda"

#. Connection inspector: label of the protected row.
msgctxt "adv_protected"
msgid "Protected"
msgstr "Protegido"

#. Network page: error when the provider list could not be loaded.
msgctxt "adv_providers_load_failed"
msgid "Could not load the provider list."
msgstr "Não foi possível carregar a lista de provedores."

#. Connection inspector (Linux) and Advanced Mode status strip (Windows): label of the raw status field.
msgctxt "adv_raw_status"
msgid "Raw status"
msgstr "Estado bruto"

#. Connection inspector: label of the decision reason row.
msgctxt "adv_reason"
msgid "Reason"
msgstr "Motivo"

#. Connection inspector: decision reason, a block override applied.
msgctxt "adv_reason_block"
msgid "Block override"
msgstr "Substituição de bloqueio"

#. Connection inspector: decision reason, the default policy applied.
msgctxt "adv_reason_default"
msgid "Default policy"
msgstr "Política padrão"

#. Connection inspector: decision reason, an override applied.
msgctxt "adv_reason_override"
msgid "Override"
msgstr "Substituição"

#. Connection inspector: decision reason, a route override applied.
msgctxt "adv_reason_route"
msgid "Route override"
msgstr "Substituição de rota"

#. Windows and Linux status strip (Advanced Mode): label of the field that shows whether the tunnel's routes are installed.
msgctxt "adv_routes"
msgid "Routes"
msgstr "Rotas"

#. Windows and Linux status strip (Advanced Mode), Routes value: routes are installed but the tunnel's DNS is not. Lowercase, a short status value.
msgctxt "adv_routes_dns_degraded"
msgid "on, dns not applied"
msgstr "ativas, DNS não aplicado"

#. Windows and Linux status strip (Advanced Mode), Routes value: no routes are installed and the kill switch is blocking traffic. Lowercase, a short status value.
msgctxt "adv_routes_kill_switch_armed"
msgid "off, kill switch armed"
msgstr "inativas, Kill switch armado"

#. Windows status strip (Advanced Mode), Routes value: routes are installed but no leak-prevention firewall policy is in force. Lowercase, a short status value.
msgctxt "adv_routes_no_firewall"
msgid "on, no leak guard"
msgstr "ativas, sem proteção contra vazamentos"

#. Windows and Linux status strip (Advanced Mode): label of the field that shows the service's RPC endpoint (host:port). RPC is a technical term.
msgctxt "adv_rpc"
msgid "RPC"
msgstr "RPC"

#. Connect page, Advanced Mode, the connection inspector and an Activity row's menu: added to a rule button's name for screen readers, after its label, while the button's rule is in force: pressing it removes the rule. Lowercase: it follows a comma.
msgctxt "adv_rule_active"
msgid "rule active, click to remove"
msgstr "regra ativa, clique para remover"

#. Connect page, Advanced Mode, the connection inspector and an Activity row's menu: the confirmation after a press removed the rule that was in force for the connection's host.
msgctxt "adv_rule_removed"
msgid "Rule removed"
msgstr "Regra removida"

#. Split rules sheet: placeholder and accessible name of the search field above the Activity list. Typing filters the list to the connections whose host name or IP address contains the text; the rules above are not filtered.
msgctxt "adv_search_activity_placeholder"
msgid "Search activity"
msgstr "Buscar na atividade"

#. Connect page, Activity pane: placeholder and accessible name of the search field above the list of connections. Typing filters the list to the connections whose host name or IP address contains the text.
msgctxt "adv_search_connections"
msgid "Search hosts or IPs"
msgstr "Buscar hosts ou IPs"

#. Connection inspector: hint to select a row in the Activity list.
msgctxt "adv_select_a_row"
msgid "Select a row in Activity to inspect it"
msgstr "Selecione uma linha em Atividade para inspecioná-la"

#. Connection inspector: suffix after the count of selected rows.
msgctxt "adv_selected"
msgid "selected"
msgstr "selecionadas"

#. Connection inspector: shown when the selected connection is no longer listed.
msgctxt "adv_selection_gone"
msgid "That connection is no longer listed"
msgstr "Essa conexão não está mais na lista"

#. Connection inspector: label of the session exit country row.
msgctxt "adv_session_exit_country"
msgid "Session exit country"
msgstr "País de saída da sessão"

#. Windows and Linux status strip (Advanced Mode): label of the field that shows which kind of session the service granted (tunnel or rpc-only).
msgctxt "adv_session_mode"
msgid "Session"
msgstr "Sessão"

#. Windows sign-in screen, first step: the quiet text link at the bottom left, beside Change Network API. It opens a sheet for signing in through the browser at ur.io with a one-time auth code.
msgctxt "adv_sign_in_browser"
msgid "Sign in with browser"
msgstr "Entrar com o navegador"

#. Split rules sheet: the one-sentence explainer at the top, above the note on network clusters. A split rule sends the chosen sites directly from this device, outside the VPN; the sheet's Activity list shows how each connection was routed.
msgctxt "adv_split_rules_note"
