#. Title of the in-app notice and of the local notification shown while the platform holds this device off because the account network already has its plan's most devices connected at once (the concurrent client limit). The device does not connect until a slot frees, the user upgrades, or the hold ends; the user's traffic stays in the tunnel. Short, like a heading.
msgctxt "client_limit_reached"
msgid "Device limit reached"
msgstr "Limite de dispositivos atingido"

#. Body under client_limit_reached, in the app and in the local notification, for a UR Pro account: it already has as many devices connected at once as its plan allows, the highest plan, so no upgrade helps. Signing out on another device frees its slot; Retry is the button beside it. Also shown when a sign-in on a new device is refused for the same limit. Keep URnetwork as it is.
msgctxt "client_limit_remove_client_message"
msgid "Your plan's limit of devices connected at once is reached. Sign out of URnetwork on a device you no longer use, then try again."
msgstr "Seu plano atingiu o limite de dispositivos conectados ao mesmo tempo. Saia do URnetwork em um dispositivo que você não usa mais e tente novamente."

#. Body under client_limit_reached, in the app and in the local notification, for an account on the free plan: it already has as many devices connected at once as the free plan allows, so this device cannot connect. UR Pro allows more; Get Pro is the button beside it. Also shown when a sign-in on a new device is refused for the same limit. Keep UR Pro and URnetwork as they are.
msgctxt "client_limit_upgrade_message"
msgid "Your free plan connects a limited number of devices at once. Upgrade to UR Pro to connect more, or disconnect URnetwork on another device."
msgstr "Seu plano gratuito conecta um número limitado de dispositivos ao mesmo tempo. Faça upgrade para o UR Pro para conectar mais ou desconecte o URnetwork em outro dispositivo."

