#. Call to action
msgctxt "kill_switch"
msgid "Kill switch"
msgstr "Kill switch"

#. Title for the disclosure explaining traffic that intentionally bypasses the VPN kill switch.
msgctxt "kill_switch_exception"
msgid "Kill switch exception"
msgstr "Exceção do Kill switch"

#. Explains the deliberate SMTP port 25 exception to the VPN kill switch, that IPv6 is routed through the tunnel, and the encrypted SMTP behavior.
msgctxt "kill_switch_exception_smtp_detail"
msgid "While the VPN is connected, IPv6 is routed through URnetwork like IPv4. Outbound SMTP on TCP port 25 bypasses the VPN, even when the kill switch is on, which may expose your local public IP to those mail servers. SMTP on ports 465 and 587 stays in the VPN and must establish TLS."
msgstr "Enquanto a VPN está conectada, o IPv6 é roteado pela URnetwork como o IPv4. O SMTP de saída na porta TCP 25 contorna a VPN, mesmo com o Kill switch ativado, o que pode expor seu IP público local a esses servidores de e-mail. O SMTP nas portas 465 e 587 fica na VPN e precisa estabelecer TLS."

#. Explains that, with the kill switch off, traffic URnetwork safety rules keep off the network (such as unrecognized encrypted protocols) bypasses the VPN.
msgctxt "kill_switch_exception_unrecognized_encrypted"
msgid "When the kill switch is off, traffic that URnetwork safety rules keep off the network, such as unrecognized encrypted protocols, bypasses the VPN and uses your local public IP. With the kill switch on, that traffic is blocked."
msgstr "Com o Kill switch desativado, o tráfego que as regras de segurança da URnetwork mantêm fora da rede, como protocolos criptografados não reconhecidos, contorna a VPN e usa seu IP público local. Com o Kill switch ativado, esse tráfego é bloqueado."

#. Button text for entering the one-time authentication code and entering the app
msgctxt "launch"
msgid "Launch"
msgstr "Iniciar"

#. Used in Main/Account/Settings/SettingsForm-macOS.swift.
msgctxt "launch_urnetwork_on_system_startup"
msgid "Launch URnetwork on system startup"
msgstr "Iniciar URnetwork na inicialização do sistema"

#. Call to action
msgctxt "leaderboard"
msgid "Leaderboard"
msgstr "Placar de Líderes"

#. Call to action
msgctxt "leaderboard_description"
msgid "The leaderboard is the sum of the last 4 payments. It is updated each payment cycle."
msgstr "O placar de líderes é a soma dos últimos 4 pagamentos. Ele é atualizado a cada ciclo de pagamento."

#. Points leaderboard: accessibility name of the draggable position indicator (a slider over ranks 1 to N).
msgctxt "leaderboard_position_indicator"
msgid "Leaderboard position"
msgstr "Posição no ranking"

#. Protocol leaderboard (Leaderboard > Protocol): own-status card, how far the network's projected score is above the Top 200 line (the score at position 200, the cutoff for a head spot). {percent} is the margin, already formatted by the app with its percent sign ("12%"), inserted as is.
msgctxt "leaderboard_protocol_above_line"
msgid "{} above the Top 200 line"
msgstr "{} acima da linha do Top 200"

#. Protocol leaderboard (Leaderboard > Protocol): the neutral one-line banner on top of the tab while claiming a Top 200 spot (binding a fleet to a miner UID on SN25) isn't open on mainnet. The board still shows where the network would rank if it claimed now.
msgctxt "leaderboard_protocol_banner_closed"
msgid "Claiming isn't open yet. You can see where you'd rank now."
msgstr "Ainda não é possível garantir vagas. Você já pode ver em que posição ficaria."

#. Protocol leaderboard (Leaderboard > Protocol): banner on top of the tab when the rankings are stale, last computed more than 3 tempos (about 3.5 hours) ago. {time} is when they were computed, already formatted by the app, a relative time ("4h ago") or a date ("Oct 29"), inserted as is, so the wording must read with either.
msgctxt "leaderboard_protocol_banner_stale"
msgid "Rankings last updated {}."
msgstr "Ranking atualizado pela última vez: {}."

#. Protocol leaderboard (Leaderboard > Protocol): own-status card, how far the network's projected score is below the Top 200 line (the score at position 200, the cutoff for a head spot). {percent} is the margin, already formatted by the app with its percent sign ("8%"), inserted as is.
msgctxt "leaderboard_protocol_below_line"
msgid "{} below the Top 200 line"
msgstr "{} abaixo da linha do Top 200"

#. Protocol leaderboard (Leaderboard > Protocol): accessibility summary of the progress chart, read by VoiceOver and TalkBack. {rank} is today's projected position, a number, inserted as is.
msgctxt "leaderboard_protocol_chart_a11y"
msgid "Projected rank over 90 days, now {}"
msgstr "Posição prevista em 90 dias, agora {}"

#. Protocol leaderboard (Leaderboard > Protocol): own-status card, label of the horizontal line drawn across the progress chart at position 200, the cutoff for a Top 200 head spot.
msgctxt "leaderboard_protocol_chart_line"
msgid "Top 200 line"
msgstr "Linha do Top 200"

#. Protocol leaderboard (Leaderboard > Protocol): own-status card, title of the progress chart: the network's projected position each day over the last 90 days.
msgctxt "leaderboard_protocol_chart_title"
msgid "Projected rank, last 90 days"
msgstr "Posição prevista, últimos 90 dias"

#. Protocol leaderboard (Leaderboard > Protocol): own-status card, added to the claim prompt when the network is within 20% of the Top 200 line. The rankings are recomputed once per tempo (about every 72 minutes).
msgctxt "leaderboard_protocol_claim_borderline"
msgid "You're close to the line, and rankings change every tempo."
msgstr "Você está perto da linha, e o ranking muda a cada tempo."

#. Protocol leaderboard (Leaderboard > Protocol): own-status card, the claim prompt's primary button once claiming is open. It opens the Earnings page (earnings) at its Top 200 tile, where the user claims the spot (claim_your_spot), so it names that page in the page's own words.
msgctxt "leaderboard_protocol_claim_button"
msgid "Claim on Earnings"
msgstr "Garantir vaga em Ganhos"

#. Protocol leaderboard (Leaderboard > Protocol): own-status card, the claim prompt for a measurable network projected inside the top 200. While claiming isn't open, leaderboard_protocol_claim_soon follows; once it opens, the Claim on Earnings button.
msgctxt "leaderboard_protocol_claim_inside"
msgid "You're projected in the top 200."
msgstr "Pela previsão, você está no Top 200."

#. Protocol leaderboard (Leaderboard > Protocol): own-status card, after "You're projected in the top 200." while claiming isn't open on mainnet. Names the Earnings page (earnings) in the page's own words. Nothing invites registering early.
msgctxt "leaderboard_protocol_claim_soon"
msgid "Claiming opens soon on the Earnings page."
msgstr "Em breve você poderá garantir sua vaga na página Ganhos."

#. Protocol leaderboard (Leaderboard > Protocol): the warning every claim prompt carries: a fleet that claimed a Top 200 spot but is ranked 201st or lower by the SN25 validator earns nothing (its devices leave the regular payout pool either way). The Earnings Top 200 tile repeats it (earnings_top200_claiming_soon_body).
msgctxt "leaderboard_protocol_claim_warning"
msgid "A claimed fleet that ranks 201 or lower earns nothing."
msgstr "Uma frota com vaga garantida que fique em 201º ou abaixo não ganha nada."

#. Protocol leaderboard (Leaderboard > Protocol): the sheet that opens from a row whose network has claimed a Top 200 spot: the state next to the fleet's UID ("UID 81 · claimed"). Lowercase where the language allows.
msgctxt "leaderboard_protocol_detail_claimed"
msgid "claimed"
msgstr "vaga garantida"

#. Protocol leaderboard (Leaderboard > Protocol): claimed row sheet, the value of Claim valid until. {epoch} is the settlement epoch number, inserted as is. Apple reads this English from the epoch_row_title entry ("Epoch %lld", one catalog entry per English text), so this key is not tagged apple.
msgctxt "leaderboard_protocol_detail_epoch"
msgid "Epoch {}"
msgstr "Época {}"

#. Protocol leaderboard (Leaderboard > Protocol): claimed row sheet, label of the generation of the fleet's binding: a number that goes up each time the fleet binds again.
msgctxt "leaderboard_protocol_detail_generation"
msgid "Generation"
msgstr "Geração"

#. Protocol leaderboard (Leaderboard > Protocol): claimed row sheet, label of the fleet UID's incentive as read from the SN25 metagraph on chain (Bittensor's incentive value, which the chain pays it by).
msgctxt "leaderboard_protocol_detail_incentive"
msgid "On-chain incentive"
msgstr "Incentivo on-chain"

#. Protocol leaderboard (Leaderboard > Protocol): claimed row sheet, note under the on-chain incentive: the chain's incentive reflects the validator's ranking one or two tempos later.
msgctxt "leaderboard_protocol_detail_incentive_note"
msgid "On-chain incentive lags the validator's ranking."
msgstr "O incentivo on-chain fica atrás do ranking do validador."

#. Protocol leaderboard (Leaderboard > Protocol): claimed row sheet: the SN25 validator did not select the fleet for a head spot in the last tempo (it was not in the validator's Top 200).
msgctxt "leaderboard_protocol_detail_not_selected"
msgid "Not selected"
msgstr "Não selecionada"

#. Protocol leaderboard (Leaderboard > Protocol): claimed row sheet, label of the network's projected position on the board.
msgctxt "leaderboard_protocol_detail_projected_rank"
msgid "Projected rank"
msgstr "Posição prevista"

#. Protocol leaderboard (Leaderboard > Protocol): claimed row sheet, label of the fleet's score as the board computes it with an exact replica of the SN25 validator's scoring, from the same measurements. Shown next to the validator's own score.
msgctxt "leaderboard_protocol_detail_replica_score"
msgid "Board replica score"
msgstr "Pontuação da réplica do placar"

#. Protocol leaderboard (Leaderboard > Protocol): claimed row sheet: the SN25 validator selected the fleet for a head spot in the last tempo (it was in the validator's Top 200).
msgctxt "leaderboard_protocol_detail_selected"
msgid "Selected"
msgstr "Selecionada"

#. Protocol leaderboard (Leaderboard > Protocol): claimed row sheet, shown next to the on-chain incentive when the value read from chain is out of date. Lowercase where the language allows.
msgctxt "leaderboard_protocol_detail_stale"
msgid "stale"
msgstr "desatualizado"

#. Protocol leaderboard (Leaderboard > Protocol): claimed row sheet, label of the last settlement epoch the fleet's claim (its binding) is valid for. The value is leaderboard_protocol_detail_epoch ("Epoch 1234").
msgctxt "leaderboard_protocol_detail_valid_until"
msgid "Claim valid until"
msgstr "Vaga garantida até"

#. Protocol leaderboard (Leaderboard > Protocol): claimed row sheet, label of where the SN25 validator itself ranked the fleet last tempo (the value is leaderboard_protocol_detail_validator_rank_value).
msgctxt "leaderboard_protocol_detail_validator_rank"
msgid "Validator rank"
msgstr "Posição no validador"

#. Protocol leaderboard (Leaderboard > Protocol): claimed row sheet, the value of Validator rank: where the SN25 validator ranked this fleet among the claimed fleets it scored last tempo. {rank} is the position and {count} the number of claimed fleets, both numbers inserted as is, so the wording must read with any number.
msgctxt "leaderboard_protocol_detail_validator_rank_value"
msgid "#{0} of {1} claimed"
msgstr "#{0} de {1} com vaga garantida"

#. Protocol leaderboard (Leaderboard > Protocol): claimed row sheet, label of the fleet's score as the SN25 validator itself computed it last tempo.
msgctxt "leaderboard_protocol_detail_validator_score"
msgid "Validator score"
msgstr "Pontuação do validador"

#. Protocol leaderboard (Leaderboard > Protocol): shown in place of the ranked list while there are no rankings yet. The board updates once per tempo, about every 72 minutes.
msgctxt "leaderboard_protocol_empty"
msgid "Rankings will appear after the next update."
msgstr "O ranking aparecerá após a próxima atualização."

#. Protocol leaderboard (Leaderboard > Protocol): the paragraph under the own-status card (in the second pane on wide screens) that explains the ranking. The SN25 validator picks its Top 200 head miners by distinct IP prefixes; a prefix several networks provide from is split between them. The board updates once per tempo, about every 72 minutes.
msgctxt "leaderboard_protocol_explainer"
msgid "Ranked the way the SN25 validator picks its Top 200: by how many distinct IP prefixes your devices provide from, with shared prefixes split between the networks on them. Updated about every 72 minutes. These are projections until you claim."
msgstr "Ranking feito do jeito que o validador da SN25 escolhe o Top 200: pelo número de prefixos de IP distintos a partir dos quais seus dispositivos fornecem, com os prefixos compartilhados divididos entre as redes que os usam. Atualizado a cada 72 minutos, aproximadamente. São previsões até você garantir sua vaga."

#. Protocol leaderboard (Leaderboard > Protocol): label chip (own-status card and own row) once the board is accurate enough: the network's projected score is within 20% of the Top 200 line, above or below it.
msgctxt "leaderboard_protocol_label_borderline"
msgid "Borderline"
msgstr "No limite"

#. Protocol leaderboard (Leaderboard > Protocol): label chip on the own-status card and the user's own row, shown until the board's measured accuracy against the validator's real picks reaches 90%: the position is only an estimate. The other chips are Likely, Borderline, Unlikely and Not measurable.
msgctxt "leaderboard_protocol_label_estimate"
msgid "Estimate"
msgstr "Estimativa"

#. Protocol leaderboard (Leaderboard > Protocol): label chip (own-status card and own row) once the board is accurate enough: the network is at least 20% above the Top 200 line and was measurable in at least 3 of the last 4 tempos, so the validator will likely rank it in its Top 200.
msgctxt "leaderboard_protocol_label_likely"
msgid "Likely"
msgstr "Provável"

#. Protocol leaderboard (Leaderboard > Protocol): label chip (own-status card and own row): the SN25 validator can't measure the network yet, so it can't score it whatever the projection says. The card says why (leaderboard_protocol_not_measurable_cohort, _shared, _providing).
msgctxt "leaderboard_protocol_label_not_measurable"
msgid "Not measurable"
msgstr "Não mensurável"

#. Protocol leaderboard (Leaderboard > Protocol): label chip (own-status card and own row) once the board is accurate enough: the network is at least 20% below the Top 200 line.
msgctxt "leaderboard_protocol_label_unlikely"
msgid "Unlikely"
msgstr "Improvável"

#. Protocol leaderboard (Leaderboard > Protocol): the divider in the ranked list between positions 200 and 201. {score} is position 200's projected score (the cutoff for a head spot), already formatted by the app ("41.2"), inserted as is.
msgctxt "leaderboard_protocol_line"
msgid "Top 200 line · score {}"
msgstr "Linha do Top 200 · pontuação {}"

#. Protocol leaderboard (Leaderboard > Protocol): what VoiceOver and TalkBack read for the divider between positions 200 and 201 (leaderboard_protocol_line). {score} is position 200's projected score, already formatted by the app ("41.2"), inserted as is.
msgctxt "leaderboard_protocol_line_a11y"
msgid "Top 200 line, score {}"
msgstr "Linha do Top 200, pontuação {}"

#. Protocol leaderboard (Leaderboard > Protocol): own-status card, why the network is not measurable: none of its devices is in the set the SN25 validator measures yet, so the validator can't score it. Shown instead of a claim prompt.
msgctxt "leaderboard_protocol_not_measurable_cohort"
msgid "Your devices aren't measured by the validator yet."
msgstr "O validador ainda não mede seus dispositivos."

#. Protocol leaderboard (Leaderboard > Protocol): own-status card, why the network is not measurable: none of its devices is providing. Shown instead of a claim prompt.
msgctxt "leaderboard_protocol_not_measurable_providing"
msgid "Turn on providing to be ranked."
msgstr "Ative o fornecimento para entrar no ranking."

#. Protocol leaderboard (Leaderboard > Protocol): own-status card, why the network is not measurable: its devices provide from an IP address another network also provides from, so the validator can't tell the two apart. Shown instead of a claim prompt.
msgctxt "leaderboard_protocol_not_measurable_shared"
msgid "Your devices share an IP with another network."
msgstr "Seus dispositivos compartilham um IP com outra rede."

#. Protocol leaderboard (Leaderboard > Protocol): own-status card, under "#173 projected": how many networks the board ranks. {count} is that number (hundreds or thousands), inserted as is, so the wording must read with any number.
msgctxt "leaderboard_protocol_of_ranked"
msgid "of {} ranked networks"
msgstr "de {} redes no ranking"

#. Protocol leaderboard (Leaderboard > Protocol): own-status card, the word after the network's position, "#173 projected": the position is a projection of where the SN25 validator would rank the network if it claimed, not a final rank. It qualifies the number before it; lowercase where the language allows.
msgctxt "leaderboard_protocol_projected"
msgid "projected"
msgstr "previsto"

#. Protocol leaderboard (Leaderboard > Protocol): own-status card, why this score: the score the network would have today if it claimed a Top 200 spot and no other network sharing its IP prefixes claimed. {score} is that score, already formatted by the app ("41.2"), inserted as is.
msgctxt "leaderboard_protocol_solo"
msgid "If you claimed alone today: {}."
msgstr "Se hoje só a sua rede garantisse vaga: {}."

#. Protocol leaderboard (Leaderboard > Protocol): own-status card, next to the trend arrow after the margin to the Top 200 line: how many positions the network moved down since the previous update (once per tempo, about every 72 minutes). {count} is the number of positions, inserted as is, so the wording must read with any number. Lowercase in English: it continues the margin line.
msgctxt "leaderboard_protocol_trend_down"
msgid "down {} since the last update"
msgstr "desceu {} desde a última atualização"

#. Protocol leaderboard (Leaderboard > Protocol): own-status card, next to the trend arrow after the margin to the Top 200 line: how many positions the network moved up since the previous update (once per tempo, about every 72 minutes). {count} is the number of positions, inserted as is, so the wording must read with any number. Lowercase in English: it continues the margin line.
msgctxt "leaderboard_protocol_trend_up"
msgid "up {} since the last update"
msgstr "subiu {} desde a última atualização"

#. Protocol leaderboard (Leaderboard > Protocol): the badge on a row whose network has claimed a Top 200 spot, and the name shown for an anonymous network that has. {uid} is the fleet's miner UID on SN25, a number, inserted as is. UID is the Bittensor term and stays as is.
msgctxt "leaderboard_protocol_uid"
msgid "UID {}"
msgstr "UID {}"

#. Protocol leaderboard (Leaderboard > Protocol): own-status card, why this score: how many distinct IP prefixes the network's devices provide from, and how many of those other networks provide from too (a shared prefix's credit is split between the networks on it). {prefixes} and {shared} are counts, each after its label and a colon, so the line reads with any number, 0 and 1 included. Counts only, never addresses.
msgctxt "leaderboard_protocol_why"
msgid "Distinct IP prefixes: {0}. Shared with other networks: {1}."
msgstr "Prefixos de IP distintos: {0}. Compartilhados com outras redes: {1}."

#. Protocol leaderboard (Leaderboard > Protocol): the marker on the signed-in network's own row in the ranked list. Apple reads this English from the route_you entry ("You", one catalog entry per English text), so this key is not tagged apple.
msgctxt "leaderboard_protocol_you"
msgid "You"
msgstr "Você"

#. Protocol leaderboard (Leaderboard > Protocol): the tab's label, the first of the leaderboard's three tabs (then Points, the points key, and Data, the data key). The tab ranks networks the way the SN25 validator picks its Top 200 head miners.
msgctxt "leaderboard_tab_protocol"
msgid "Protocol"
msgstr "Protocolo"

#. Points leaderboard scroll indicator: the tier line for ranks below the top 50%.
msgctxt "leaderboard_tier_rest"
msgid "Everyone else"
msgstr "Todos os outros"

#. Points leaderboard scroll indicator: the tier line under the rank while dragging; {percent} is 1, 5, 10, 25 or 50.
