msgctxt "site_install_app"
msgid "Install the app"
msgstr "Instalar o app"

#. Instant account creation: error when the server returned no seedphrase for the new account.
msgctxt "site_instant_no_seedphrase"
msgid "The account was created without a recoverable seedphrase. Please contact support."
msgstr "A conta foi criada sem uma frase-semente recuperável. Entre em contato com o suporte."

#. Instant account creation: hint that the seedphrase is the only way to recover the account.
msgctxt "site_instant_seedphrase_only_recovery"
msgid "No email or password is needed. A 24-word seedphrase is the only way to recover the account."
msgstr "Não é preciso e-mail nem senha. Uma frase-semente de 24 palavras é a única forma de recuperar a conta."

#. Login stack: hint above the seedphrase field when signing in with an instant account's seed.
msgctxt "site_login_seed_hint"
msgid "Enter the 24-word seedphrase shown when the instant account was created."
msgstr "Digite a frase-semente de 24 palavras exibida quando a conta instantânea foi criada."

#. Login stack: error when the entered seed does not match an account.
msgctxt "site_login_seed_not_recognized"
msgid "Seed not recognized."
msgstr "Semente não reconhecida."

#. Login stack: tooltip on the Seed tile, signing in with an instant account's seed.
msgctxt "site_login_seed_title"
msgid "Sign in with the seed of an instant account"
msgstr "Entrar com a semente de uma conta instantânea"

#. Login stack: title of the seed sign-in view.
msgctxt "site_login_seed_view_title"
msgid "Sign in with Seed"
msgstr "Entrar com semente"

#. Account panel: the small button on the plan card that opens Manage Subscription in the app.
msgctxt "site_manage"
msgid "Manage"
msgstr "Gerenciar"

#. Account panel: hint under the plan card for Pro members, next to the Manage button that opens Manage Subscription.
msgctxt "site_manage_subscription_hint"
msgid "See your renewal date, auto-renew status and cancel options."
msgstr "Veja a data de renovação, a renovação automática e as opções de cancelamento."

#. ur.io Connect screen, out-of-balance notice: what the browser does meanwhile when the URnetwork extension's kill switch is off (its default). The extension then takes its proxy off after failed health checks (or, in Firefox, sends each request directly), so the browser goes online without URnetwork. Keep URnetwork as is; translate kill switch as the extension and the apps do.
msgctxt "site_out_of_data_browser_direct"
msgid "With the kill switch off, the extension soon lets this browser connect directly, without URnetwork."
msgstr "Com o kill switch desligado, a extensão em breve deixa este navegador se conectar diretamente, sem o URnetwork."

#. ur.io Connect screen, out-of-balance notice: what the browser does meanwhile when the URnetwork extension's kill switch is on. The extension keeps its proxy set, so pages fail until data is available again or the user disconnects. Translate kill switch as the extension and the apps do.
msgctxt "site_out_of_data_browser_held"
msgid "With the kill switch on, pages won't load in this browser until data is available or you disconnect."
msgstr "Com o kill switch ligado, as páginas não carregam neste navegador até haver dados disponíveis ou você desconectar."

#. Checkout (ur.io's payment screens; the plan purchase in the F-Droid and dapp Android builds; the upgrade sheet in the macOS direct download, Windows and Linux): the server refused a new subscription because the network already has an active Pro subscription (error.code already_subscribed). Nothing was charged.
msgctxt "site_payment_error_already_subscribed"
msgid "You already have Pro, so nothing was charged. Manage your subscription from your account."
msgstr "Você já tem o Pro, então nada foi cobrado. Gerencie sua assinatura na sua conta."

#. Checkout (ur.io's payment screens; the plan purchase in the F-Droid and dapp Android builds; the upgrade sheet in the macOS direct download, Windows and Linux): the server cannot sell this Pro plan right now (error.code plan_unavailable: no price or product is configured for it). Nothing was charged.
msgctxt "site_payment_error_plan_unavailable"
msgid "This plan is not available right now. Try again later."
msgstr "Este plano não está disponível no momento. Tente novamente mais tarde."

#. Instant account creation: heading of the view that shows the new seedphrase once.
msgctxt "site_save_your_seedphrase"
msgid "Save Your Seedphrase"
msgstr "Salve sua frase-semente"

#. Instant account creation: the clipboard copy of the seedphrase failed.
msgctxt "site_seedphrase_copy_failed"
msgid "Could not copy the seedphrase. Select and copy the words below."
msgstr "Não foi possível copiar a frase-semente. Selecione e copie as palavras abaixo."

#. Subscription: date line when the store did not answer whether it auto-renews. {date} is a localized date.
msgctxt "site_sub_active_until"
msgid "Active until {date}"
msgstr "Ativa até {date}"

#. Subscription: status chip — the subscription will not renew itself.
msgctxt "site_sub_auto_renew_off"
msgid "Auto-renew off"
msgstr "Renovação automática desativada"

#. Subscription: status chip — the subscription renews itself.
msgctxt "site_sub_auto_renew_on"
msgid "Auto-renew on"
msgstr "Renovação automática ativada"

#. Subscription: status chip — the store did not answer whether it auto-renews.
msgctxt "site_sub_auto_renew_unknown"
msgid "Auto-renew unknown"
msgstr "Renovação automática desconhecida"

#. Subscription: store sentence for a Pro year paid with USDC on Solana.
msgctxt "site_sub_billed_solana"
msgid "Paid with USDC on Solana."
msgstr "Pago com USDC na Solana."

#. Subscription: secondary link that opens Stripe's billing portal (payment details, invoices). Shown only when the network has a Stripe customer.
msgctxt "site_sub_billing_details"
msgid "Billing details"
msgstr "Dados de cobrança"

#. Subscription: the cancel button for a Stripe-billed subscription (cancels at the end of the paid period).
msgctxt "site_sub_cancel"
msgid "Cancel subscription"
msgstr "Cancelar assinatura"

#. Subscription: inline confirmation before cancelling. {date} is the end of the paid period, a localized date.
msgctxt "site_sub_cancel_confirm"
msgid "Cancel at the end of the period? You keep Pro until {date}."
msgstr "Cancelar no fim do período? Você mantém o Pro até {date}."

#. Subscription: back out of the cancellation.
msgctxt "site_sub_cancel_keep"
msgid "Keep it"
msgstr "Manter"

#. Subscription: inline confirmation before cancelling a renewal whose payment is failing. The cancel takes effect now: Stripe stops retrying the failed payment, and the Pro plan ends. Retrying = Stripe trying to charge the card again.
msgctxt "site_sub_cancel_past_due_confirm"
msgid "Cancel now? We'll stop retrying your payment, and Pro ends."
msgstr "Cancelar agora? Vamos parar de tentar o pagamento de novo, e o Pro termina."

#. Subscription: confirm the cancellation.
msgctxt "site_sub_cancel_yes"
msgid "Yes, cancel"
msgstr "Sim, cancelar"

#. Subscription: a cancel or resume request failed.
msgctxt "site_sub_change_error"
msgid "Could not update the subscription. Please try again."
msgstr "Não foi possível atualizar a assinatura. Tente novamente."

#. Subscription: shown when the details request (dates, auto-renew) failed and the screen falls back to the list of billing stores.
msgctxt "site_sub_details_error"
msgid "Could not load the renewal details. Showing what we know."
msgstr "Não foi possível carregar os detalhes da renovação. Mostrando o que sabemos."

#. Subscription: date line when auto-renew is off (cancelled, or a one-time USDC year). {date} is a localized date.
msgctxt "site_sub_ends_on"
msgid "Ends on {date}"
msgstr "Termina em {date}"

#. Subscription: free plan body
msgctxt "site_sub_free_body"
msgid "You're on the Free plan. Upgrade to Pro for more data and features."
msgstr "Você está no plano Free. Mude para Pro para ter mais dados e recursos."

#. Subscription: free plan title
msgctxt "site_sub_free_title"
msgid "Free plan"
msgstr "Plano Free"

#. Subscription: manage-on-platform button ({platform})
msgctxt "site_sub_manage_on"
msgid "Manage in {platform}"
msgstr "Gerenciar em {platform}"

#. Subscription: manage-on-platform button, Apple. A full sentence rather than interpolating the store name, because the article and case around it differ per language.
msgctxt "site_sub_manage_on_apple"
msgid "Manage in the App Store"
msgstr "Gerenciar na App Store"

#. Subscription: manage-on-platform button, Google. A full sentence rather than interpolating the store name, because the article and case around it differ per language.
msgctxt "site_sub_manage_on_google"
msgid "Manage in Google Play"
msgstr "Gerenciar no Google Play"

#. Subscription: unknown platform fallback
msgctxt "site_sub_other_platform"
msgid "another platform"
msgstr "outra plataforma"

#. ur.io Manage subscription: the past-due notice under its title. Stripe retries the failed renewal for about two weeks, then cancels the subscription. The notice's two actions are "Update payment method" and "Pay invoice" (the failing invoice, paid with another card). Keep UR Pro and Pro (the plan's name) unchanged.
msgctxt "site_sub_past_due_body"
msgid "We couldn't renew UR Pro with your payment method. Update your payment method, or pay the invoice with another card, to keep Pro."
msgstr "Não conseguimos renovar o UR Pro com sua forma de pagamento. Atualize sua forma de pagamento ou pague a fatura com outro cartão para continuar com o Pro."

#. ur.io Manage subscription: title of the notice shown while a Stripe renewal's payment has failed (a declined card, for example) and Stripe is retrying it. Didn't go through = failed.
msgctxt "site_sub_past_due_title"
msgid "Your payment didn't go through"
msgstr "Seu pagamento não foi concluído"

#. ur.io Manage subscription: button on the past-due notice that opens the failing renewal's invoice on Stripe's own page, where it can be paid at once with another card.
msgctxt "site_sub_pay_invoice"
msgid "Pay invoice"
msgstr "Pagar fatura"

#. Subscription: other-platform body ({platform})
msgctxt "site_sub_platform_body"
msgid "Your Pro subscription is billed through {platform}. To change or cancel it, manage your subscriptions in {platform}."
msgstr "Sua assinatura Pro é cobrada através de {platform}. Para alterá-la ou cancelá-la, gerencie suas assinaturas através de {platform}."

#. Subscription: billing explanation, Apple. Full sentence so each language can inflect around the store name naturally.
msgctxt "site_sub_platform_body_apple"
msgid "Your Pro subscription is billed through the App Store. To change or cancel it, manage your subscriptions in the App Store."
msgstr "Sua assinatura Pro é cobrada através da App Store. Para alterá-la ou cancelá-la, gerencie suas assinaturas na App Store."

#. Subscription: billing explanation, Google. Full sentence so each language can inflect around the store name naturally.
msgctxt "site_sub_platform_body_google"
msgid "Your Pro subscription is billed through Google Play. To change or cancel it, manage your subscriptions in Google Play."
msgstr "Sua assinatura Pro é cobrada através do Google Play. Para alterá-la ou cancelá-la, gerencie suas assinaturas no Google Play."

#. Subscription: date line when auto-renew is on. {date} is a localized date.
msgctxt "site_sub_renews_on"
msgid "Renews on {date}"
msgstr "Renova em {date}"

#. Subscription: undo a pending cancellation while the paid period is still running.
msgctxt "site_sub_resume"
msgid "Resume subscription"
msgstr "Retomar assinatura"

#. Subscription: note under a USDC-paid year — it is a one-time payment with nothing to cancel.
msgctxt "site_sub_solana_no_renew"
msgid "Does not renew. Pay again with USDC on Solana when it ends."
msgstr "Não renova. Pague novamente com USDC na Solana quando terminar."

#. Subscription: Stripe-billed body
msgctxt "site_sub_stripe_body"
msgid "Your Pro subscription is billed through Stripe. Update your payment details or cancel anytime below."
msgstr "Sua assinatura Pro é cobrada através da Stripe. Atualize os dados de pagamento ou cancele quando quiser abaixo."

#. Manage subscription (ur.io's screen; Settings in the Windows app, Account in the Linux app), opening the billing details: the network has no Stripe customer, so there is no billing portal (error.code no_customer).
msgctxt "site_subscription_error_no_customer"
msgid "This network has no Stripe billing details."
msgstr "Esta rede não tem dados de cobrança no Stripe."

#. Manage subscription (ur.io's screen; Settings in the Windows app, Account in the Linux app): Stripe did not answer or refused the change, or the billing portal could not be opened; trying again usually works (error.code store_unavailable).
msgctxt "site_subscription_error_store_unavailable"
msgid "Stripe could not be reached just now. Try again in a moment."
msgstr "Não foi possível acessar o Stripe agora. Tente novamente em instantes."

#. Upgrade sheet: the win-back offer line while a returning subscriber's offer is active (the monthly plan's first month at a discount). {percent} whole number, {when} a local date and time.
msgctxt "site_winback_sheet_line"
msgid "Welcome back: {0}% off your first month, until {1}"
msgstr "Oferta de retorno: {0}% de desconto no primeiro mês, até {1}"

#. Small muted button at the top of the post-login onboarding flow that leaves the whole flow.
msgctxt "skip"
msgid "Skip"
msgstr "Pular"

#. Status label while the user's own network is slowing traffic (URnetwork measured a high upload or download delay). Shown in the amber pill at the top of the connect screen (also the Mac toolbar and menu bar, and the Windows and Linux connect page), as the title of the details sheet that pill opens, as the Live Activity title on the iPhone Lock Screen and expanded Dynamic Island, and as the Android VPN notification title. It describes the user's internet connection, not a URnetwork fault. Keep it short: it sits in a small pill beside an icon.
msgctxt "slow_internet"
msgid "Slow internet"
msgstr "Internet lenta"

#. Label for the measured download delay (for example 640 ms or 1.2 s, with the download rate when it is limited) in the slow-internet details sheet, the expanded Dynamic Island and Lock Screen Live Activity, the Android VPN notification, and the Windows and Linux tray and notification. Download = traffic this device receives. Keep it short: it labels a number in a small box.
msgctxt "slow_internet_download_delay"
msgid "Download delay"
msgstr "Atraso no download"

#. Replaces "Slow internet" in the connect-screen pill when URnetwork itself is the reason traffic is slower: it switched to a slower fallback (backup) connection because its usual connection is blocked or unavailable on this network. Keep it short: it sits in a small pill beside an icon.
msgctxt "slow_internet_fallback"
msgid "Fallback connection"
msgstr "Conexão alternativa"

#. Body text of the slow-internet details sheet (a flyout on Windows and Linux) while URnetwork is on a slower fallback (backup) connection. Its usual connection = the way URnetwork normally connects, which this network blocks or does not support.
msgctxt "slow_internet_fallback_body"
msgid "URnetwork is using a slower fallback connection because its usual connection isn't available on this network."
msgstr "A URnetwork está usando uma conexão alternativa mais lenta porque a conexão habitual não está disponível nesta rede."

#. Replaces "Poor signal" in the small pill at the top right of the connect screen on iPhone, iPad, Mac, Android, Windows and Linux while URnetwork carries the traffic over a slower fallback (backup) connection, because its usual connection is blocked or unavailable on this network. A status tag beside a small tunnel icon and the delay numbers: one short word, two at most.
msgctxt "slow_internet_fallback_short"
msgid "Fallback"
msgstr "Modo alternativo"

#. Title of the slow-internet details sheet, the iPhone Live Activity and the Android VPN notification while URnetwork is on a slower fallback (backup) connection because its usual connection isn't available on the current network. Replaces "Slow internet" in that case.
msgctxt "slow_internet_fallback_title"
msgid "Using a slower fallback connection"
msgstr "Usando uma conexão alternativa mais lenta"

#. Settings switch on Windows (Settings > General), Linux, and iPhone (in Settings): when on (the default), the app shows a notification, once per episode, when the user's internet becomes slow.
msgctxt "slow_internet_notify_toggle"
msgid "Notify me when my internet is slow"
msgstr "Avisar quando minha internet estiver lenta"

#. Label in the small pill at the top right of the connect screen on iPhone, iPad, Mac, Android, Windows and Linux, shown while the user's own internet connection is slow or congested: URnetwork measured a long upload or download delay. It sits in amber beside a small tunnel icon and the delay numbers (for example ↑ 800 ms ↓ 1.9 s). It describes the user's network, Wi-Fi, cellular or wired alike, not a URnetwork fault. Use your language's usual short phrase for a poor connection signal, one or two words: the pill has very little room.
msgctxt "slow_internet_poor_signal"
msgid "Poor signal"
msgstr "Sinal fraco"

#. Title shown for about 3 seconds when a slow-internet episode ends, just before the indicator goes away: in the iPhone Live Activity (Lock Screen and Dynamic Island), the Android VPN notification, and the Windows and Linux notification.
msgctxt "slow_internet_recovered"
msgid "Internet back to normal"
msgstr "A internet voltou ao normal"

#. Subtitle under "Internet back to normal" in the brief recovered state at the end of a slow-internet episode: the upload and download delays URnetwork measured are gone.
msgctxt "slow_internet_recovered_detail"
msgid "Delays cleared"
msgstr "Os atrasos acabaram"

#. The one-word form of "Slow internet" in the iPhone Dynamic Island's compact view (trailing side, beside the small tunnel icon, in amber). There is room for only a few characters, so use the shortest natural word for slow.
msgctxt "slow_internet_short"
msgid "Slow"
msgstr "Lenta"

#. Subtitle under the slow-internet title in the iPhone Live Activity and the Android VPN notification: reassures the user that the VPN has not dropped even though traffic is slow.
msgctxt "slow_internet_still_connected"
msgid "URnetwork is still connected"
msgstr "A URnetwork continua conectada"

#. Label for the measured upload delay (for example 640 ms or 1.2 s, with the upload rate when it is limited) in the slow-internet details sheet, the expanded Dynamic Island and Lock Screen Live Activity, the Android VPN notification, and the Windows and Linux tray and notification. Upload = traffic this device sends. Keep it short: it labels a number in a small box.
msgctxt "slow_internet_upload_delay"
msgid "Upload delay"
msgstr "Atraso no upload"

#. The subnet alpha token symbol.
msgctxt "sn_alpha_symbol"
msgid "SN25α"
msgstr "SN25α"

#. Earnings, the settlement v2 tile and the claim sheet: a Claim now for this address went through, so the next one opens on this date, 30 days after that claim went through (the limit the queued note names). The placeholder is a date, as Dec 3. Claim now is the button's label; keep it recognizable as that label.
msgctxt "sn_claim_relay_again_on"
msgid "Your next Claim now opens on {}."
msgstr "O próximo “Resgatar agora” fica disponível em {}."

#. Earnings, the settlement v2 tile and the claim sheet: URnetwork's daily budget for paying claim gas is spent, so the claim waits. The budget renews every day at 00:00 UTC, and a waiting claim goes out once a day's budget reaches it, which can be later than the next day. Say nothing that promises a day, and keep 00:00 and UTC.
msgctxt "sn_claim_relay_cap"
msgid "Today's claim budget is used up, so this waits. The budget renews each day at 00:00 UTC. Nothing is lost: this credit never expires."
msgstr "O orçamento de resgates de hoje se esgotou, então isso aguarda. O orçamento se renova todos os dias às 00:00 UTC. Nada se perde: este saldo nunca expira."

#. Earnings, the settlement v2 tile and the claim sheet: a button that asks URnetwork to claim the balance now, without waiting for the automatic threshold. Short: a button.
msgctxt "sn_claim_relay_claim_now"
msgid "Claim now"
msgstr "Resgatar agora"

#. Earnings, the settlement v2 tile, under the Claim now button: URnetwork pays the gas, and the button can be used once in this many days (30 today; the count selects the plural form). Claim now is the button's label; keep it recognizable as that label.
msgctxt "sn_claim_relay_claim_now_paid"
msgid "Claim now is paid by URnetwork, once a day."
msgid_plural "Claim now is paid by URnetwork, once every {} days."
msgstr[0] "“Resgatar agora” é pago pelo URnetwork, uma vez por dia."
msgstr[1] "“Resgatar agora” é pago pelo URnetwork, uma vez a cada {} dias."

#. Earnings claim sheet, under the Claim now button: URnetwork pays the gas, once in this many days (30 today; the count selects the plural form) for each Bittensor address (coldkey). Keep coldkey as the app writes it elsewhere.
msgctxt "sn_claim_relay_claim_now_paid_each"
msgid "Paid by URnetwork, once a day for each coldkey."
msgid_plural "Paid by URnetwork, once every {} days for each coldkey."
msgstr[0] "Pago pelo URnetwork, uma vez por dia para cada coldkey."
msgstr[1] "Pago pelo URnetwork, uma vez a cada {} dias para cada coldkey."

#. Earnings, the claim sheet and the settlement v2 tile, once URnetwork has claimed the balance and paid the gas (the claimed state, beside a link to the transaction). The first placeholder is the amount claimed, as 0.8420; the second is the user's Bittensor address, shortened (5F3s…kQ9v); keep both as they are.
msgctxt "sn_claim_relay_claimed"
msgid "Claimed by URnetwork. {0} SN25α is on your key, {1}."
msgstr "Resgatado pelo URnetwork. {0} SN25α estão na sua chave, {1}."

#. Earnings screen, the settlement v2 tile and the claim sheet: a line beside a relay icon. URnetwork sends the claim transaction and pays its gas; the SN25α goes to the user's own address.
msgctxt "sn_claim_relay_for_you"
msgid "URnetwork claims this for you"
msgstr "O URnetwork resgata isso para você"

#. Earnings claim sheet: who claims and where the tokens go. The placeholder is the user's Bittensor address, shortened (5F3s…kQ9v); keep it as it is.
msgctxt "sn_claim_relay_lands_on"
msgid "URnetwork claims this for you. It pays the gas, and your SN25α lands on {}."
msgstr "O URnetwork resgata isso para você. Ele paga o gás, e seu SN25α chega a {}."

#. Earnings, the settlement v2 tile and the claim sheet: URnetwork isn't sending claims at the moment.
msgctxt "sn_claim_relay_not_running"
msgid "Automatic claims aren't running right now."
msgstr "Os resgates automáticos não estão funcionando no momento."

#. Earnings, the settlement v2 tile and the claim sheet: URnetwork paused claims for everyone for a while.
msgctxt "sn_claim_relay_paused"
msgid "URnetwork has paused claims for now."
msgstr "O URnetwork pausou os resgates por enquanto."

#. Earnings, the settlement v2 tile and the claim sheet: why the balance is still pending, it is in line to be claimed.
msgctxt "sn_claim_relay_queued"
msgid "URnetwork claims this soon."
msgstr "O URnetwork vai resgatar isso em breve."

#. Earnings claim sheet: the Claim now button, disabled, after the claim was asked for. Short: a button.
msgctxt "sn_claim_relay_queued_button"
msgid "Queued"
msgstr "Na fila"

#. Earnings, the settlement v2 tile and the claim sheet: the last claim transaction failed, and URnetwork will try again by itself.
msgctxt "sn_claim_relay_refused"
msgid "The last claim didn't go through. URnetwork tries again later."
msgstr "O último resgate não foi concluído. O URnetwork vai tentar de novo mais tarde."

#. Earnings, the settlement v2 tile and the claim sheet, after the user tapped Claim now: the claim is in line. URnetwork sends tapped claims before its automatic ones, the oldest request first, as far as each day's gas budget reaches, so it can go out today or on a later day. Say nothing that promises a day. Claim now is the button's label; keep it recognizable as that label.
msgctxt "sn_claim_relay_requested"
msgid "Claim now is queued. It goes out ahead of automatic claims, in the order requests came in, as each day's budget allows."
msgstr "“Resgatar agora” está na fila. Ele é enviado antes dos resgates automáticos, na ordem em que os pedidos chegaram, dentro do orçamento de cada dia."

#. Earnings, the settlement v2 tile and the claim sheet, under the queued Claim now: the Claim now limit (once in this many days, 30 today; the count selects the plural form) starts when URnetwork's claim of this balance is paid, not at the tap, so the next Claim now opens this many days after this claim goes through. Claim now is the button's label; keep it recognizable as that label.
msgctxt "sn_claim_relay_requested_period"
msgid "Your next Claim now opens a day after this claim goes through."
msgid_plural "Your next Claim now opens {} days after this claim goes through."
msgstr[0] "O próximo “Resgatar agora” fica disponível um dia depois que este resgate for concluído."
msgstr[1] "O próximo “Resgatar agora” fica disponível {} dias depois que este resgate for concluído."

#. Earnings, the settlement v2 tile and the claim sheet: a link to claim the balance from this device, paying the gas with the user's gas key (a small TAO account on this device). Keep gas key as the app writes it elsewhere.
msgctxt "sn_claim_relay_self_claim"
msgid "Claim it yourself with your gas key"
msgstr "Resgate você mesmo com sua chave de gás"

#. Earnings, the settlement v2 tile and the claim sheet: why Claim now can't be used yet. The placeholder is the smallest amount, in TAO (0.0001).
msgctxt "sn_claim_relay_under_floor"
msgid "Claim now needs a balance worth at least {} TAO."
msgstr "“Resgatar agora” requer um saldo no valor de pelo menos {} TAO."

#. Earnings, the settlement v2 tile and the claim sheet: why the balance is still pending. URnetwork claims automatically once a balance is worth a set amount.
msgctxt "sn_claim_relay_under_threshold"
msgid "Below the automatic threshold."
msgstr "Abaixo do limite de resgate automático."

#. Earnings, the settlement v2 tile and the claim sheet, under Below the automatic threshold. The placeholders are amounts: the threshold in TAO (0.0125), then the same in SN25α at today's price (3).
msgctxt "sn_claim_relay_under_threshold_body"
msgid "It's claimed for you once it's worth about {0} TAO, about {1} SN25α at today's price. Waiting costs nothing: this credit never expires."
msgstr "É resgatado em seu nome assim que valer cerca de {0} TAO, cerca de {1} SN25α pelo preço de hoje. Esperar não custa nada: este saldo nunca expira."

#. Earnings, the settlement v2 tile and the claim sheet, under Below the automatic threshold, when today's SN25α price isn't known. The placeholder is the threshold in TAO (0.0125).
msgctxt "sn_claim_relay_under_threshold_no_price"
msgid "It's claimed for you once it's worth about {} TAO. Waiting costs nothing: this credit never expires."
msgstr "É resgatado em seu nome assim que valer cerca de {} TAO. Esperar não custa nada: este saldo nunca expira."

#. Earnings, the settlement v2 tile and the claim sheet, under Automatic claims aren't running right now: nothing is lost. The vault is the settlement contract holding the user's balance.
msgctxt "sn_claim_relay_waits"
msgid "Your SN25α waits in the vault, and this credit never expires."
msgstr "Seu SN25α aguarda no cofre e este saldo nunca expira."

#. Earnings, the settlement v2 tile and the claim sheet, when URnetwork isn't claiming: the link below claims with the user's own gas key. Ends with a colon before that link.
msgctxt "sn_claim_relay_waits_for_relay"
msgid "Claim now waits until claims are running again. To claim right away, pay the gas yourself:"
msgstr "“Resgatar agora” aguarda até os resgates voltarem a funcionar. Para resgatar agora mesmo, pague o gás você mesmo:"

#. Payout consent section, beside the settlement v2 tile and claim: the status while a consent covers the current epoch. The placeholder is the consented Bittensor coldkey, shortened to its first and last four characters around an ellipsis (5F3s…kQ9v); keep it as is.
msgctxt "sn_consent_active"
msgid "Earnings are paid to {}"
msgstr "Os ganhos são pagos para {}"

#. Payout consent section, beside the settlement v2 tile and claim: the explanation under the status. One signature with the Bittensor wallet's coldkey covers every provider client of the network.
msgctxt "sn_consent_body"
msgid "Sign once with your Bittensor wallet so this network's earnings are paid to it."
msgstr "Assine uma vez com sua carteira Bittensor para que os ganhos desta rede sejam pagos nela."

#. Payout consent section, beside the settlement v2 tile and claim: the button shown while a consent is active. It reruns the signing with another Bittensor wallet.
msgctxt "sn_consent_change"
msgid "Change wallet"
msgstr "Trocar carteira"

#. Payout consent section, beside the settlement v2 tile and claim: the note with Change wallet (sn_consent_change) while a consent is active. An epoch is the settlement period, about 7 days.
msgctxt "sn_consent_change_note"
msgid "A new wallet takes effect from the next epoch."
msgstr "Uma nova carteira passa a valer a partir da próxima época."

#. Payout consent section, beside the settlement v2 tile and claim: the error when the consent message expired (300 seconds after the server issued it) before the signed consent reached the server. Trying again requests a new message.
msgctxt "sn_consent_expired"
msgid "The request expired. Try again."
msgstr "A solicitação expirou. Tente novamente."

#. Payout consent section, beside the settlement v2 tile and claim: the error when the server refused the signature because it does not verify for the wallet's coldkey (SnErrorCodeSignatureMismatch).
msgctxt "sn_consent_failed"
msgid "The signature didn't match this wallet. Try again."
msgstr "A assinatura não corresponde a esta carteira. Tente novamente."

#. Payout consent section, beside the settlement v2 tile and claim: the status while no consent covers the current epoch, so the network's earnings are not paid. The Sign with wallet button (sn_consent_sign) follows.
msgctxt "sn_consent_none"
msgid "No payout wallet yet. Earnings aren't paid until you sign."
msgstr "Ainda não há carteira de pagamento. Os ganhos só são pagos depois que você assinar."

#. Payout consent section, beside the settlement v2 tile and claim: the error when the signed-in session is not the network owner's. Only the owner chooses where the network's earnings are paid.
msgctxt "sn_consent_owner_only"
msgid "Only the network owner can choose the payout wallet."
msgstr "Somente o proprietário da rede pode escolher a carteira de pagamento."

#. Payout consent section, beside the settlement v2 tile and claim: the button shown while no consent is active. It connects the Bittensor wallet, which then signs the consent message the server issued.
msgctxt "sn_consent_sign"
msgid "Sign with wallet"
msgstr "Assinar com a carteira"

#. Payout consent section, beside the settlement v2 tile and claim: the progress line while the Bittensor wallet is asked to sign the consent message.
msgctxt "sn_consent_signing"
msgid "Waiting for your wallet's signature…"
msgstr "Aguardando a assinatura da sua carteira…"

#. Payout consent section, beside the settlement v2 tile and claim: its title. The network owner signs once with a Bittensor wallet, and that coldkey is paid the earnings of every provider client of the network.
msgctxt "sn_consent_title"
msgid "Payout consent"
msgstr "Consentimento de pagamento"

#. Earnings, the settlement v2 tile, the claim sheet and the claim dialog: names the coldkey's account in URnetwork's capture the flag pool (an account whose kind is ctf), in place of Pool {no_id} (sn_ledger_pool). Capture the flag is a draw in each country: each epoch it picks up to five of the providers and up to five of the extenders that were online there for at least half the epoch, and pays them SN25α into this account. A short title: use your language's name for the game capture the flag, never the hacking contest.
msgctxt "sn_ctf_pool"
msgid "Capture the flag"
msgstr "Capture a bandeira"

#. Earnings, with the capture the flag account (sn_ctf_pool): a line saying a capture the flag draw gave this device one of a country's five extender slots (GET /sn/ctf/client). Up to five devices win a role's slots, and a flag counts as held only once all ten of a country's slots are won, so say the device won a slot, never that it captured or holds the flag. The placeholder is the country's name exactly as the app shows it, e.g. Kenya, with no case ending or article added, so keep it where the bare name reads correctly (several languages lead with it: "{country}: ..."). Mention no amount.
msgctxt "sn_ctf_won_extender_slot"
msgid "You won one of the {} extender slots"
msgstr "{}: você ganhou uma das vagas de extensor"

#. Earnings, with the capture the flag account (sn_ctf_pool): a line saying a capture the flag draw gave this device one of a country's five provider slots (GET /sn/ctf/client). Up to five devices win a role's slots, and a flag counts as held only once all ten of a country's slots are won, so say the device won a slot, never that it captured or holds the flag. The placeholder is the country's name exactly as the app shows it, e.g. Kenya, with no case ending or article added, so keep it where the bare name reads correctly (several languages lead with it: "{country}: ..."). Mention no amount.
msgctxt "sn_ctf_won_provider_slot"
msgid "You won one of the {} provider slots"
msgstr "{}: você ganhou uma das vagas de provedor"

#. Windows Earnings page, the ledger header's Earnings actions menu (which repeats the page's actions while the window is too narrow to show them): the item for settlement v2's claim, which opens its claim dialog. Keep "v2".
msgctxt "sn_ledger_claim"
msgid "Claim settlement v2"
msgstr "Resgatar liquidação v2"

#. Earnings, the settlement v2 tile and the claim dialog: the one button that claims the coldkey's provider pool account (sn_ledger_provider_pool) and its capture the flag account (sn_ctf_pool) together, while both are claimable. The device sends the two claims in one transaction. Claim now, URnetwork's own button, keeps its label and claims both pools too. Short: a button.
msgctxt "sn_ledger_claim_both"
msgid "Claim both"
msgstr "Resgatar ambos"

#. Settlement v2 tile: label of the SN25α the user can claim now.
msgctxt "sn_ledger_claimable"
msgid "Claimable"
msgstr "Disponível para resgate"

#. Settlement v2 tile: label of the SN25α earned so far (finalized: paid plus claimable).
msgctxt "sn_ledger_earned"
msgid "Earned"
msgstr "Ganho"

#. Settlement v2 tile: label of the SN25α already paid to the user's coldkey.
msgctxt "sn_ledger_paid"
msgid "Paid"
msgstr "Pago"

#. Settlement v2 tile: earnings committed but not final yet. {} is an SN25α amount, e.g. "0.7500 SN25α".
msgctxt "sn_ledger_pending"
msgid "Pending: +{}, awaiting finalization"
msgstr "Pendente: +{}, aguardando finalização"

#. Settlement v2 tile and claim dialog: names an operator pool. {} is its number.
msgctxt "sn_ledger_pool"
msgid "Pool {}"
msgstr "Pool {}"

#. Earnings, the settlement v2 tile and the claim sheet: shown in one pool's row in place of its balances, never a zero, when the server lists that pool in unavailable_pools (its ledger could not be read just now). The other pools' rows show as usual. The tile's Unavailable (sn_ledger_unavailable) stays for when no balance can be read at all.
msgctxt "sn_ledger_pool_unavailable"
msgid "Unavailable right now"
msgstr "Indisponível no momento"

#. Earnings, the settlement v2 tile and the claim sheet: the status of one pool's account, in its row where Pending or Claimed would be, while its balance is under the transfer floor, the smallest amount the chain lets a claim move (sn_claim_relay_under_floor gives it in TAO). Neither URnetwork's claim nor the device's can claim it until it is worth at least that; it waits in the vault, and this credit never expires. A capture the flag account is often this small. Short: a status. Say nothing about when it becomes claimable.
msgctxt "sn_ledger_pool_under_floor"
msgid "Below the claim minimum"
msgstr "Abaixo do mínimo para resgatar"

#. Earnings, the settlement v2 tile, the claim sheet and the claim dialog: names the coldkey's account in URnetwork's provider pool (an account whose kind is provider) beside its capture the flag account (sn_ctf_pool), in place of Pool {no_id} (sn_ledger_pool). The provider pool is the settlement v2 pool that pays for the network's usage and the extenders' share. A short title; use the app's word for provider and for pool.
msgctxt "sn_ledger_provider_pool"
msgid "Provider pool"
msgstr "Pool de provedores"

#. Title of the settlement v2 tile, and the caption of its claim dialog's total. Keep "v2".
msgctxt "sn_ledger_title"
msgid "Settlement v2"
msgstr "Liquidação v2"

#. Settlement v2 tile: shown instead of the balances when they cannot be read, never a zero.
msgctxt "sn_ledger_unavailable"
msgid "Unavailable"
msgstr "Indisponível"

#. Earnings card: how providers are paid on the UR subnet (WHITEPAPER §5.2, §8.3). Earnings settle per epoch and are paid in SN25α as stake to the provider's Bittensor coldkey once the provider claims them; nothing is paid automatically. Followed by sn_payout_schedule_times when the epoch schedule is known.
msgctxt "sn_payout_schedule"
msgid "Earnings settle every epoch and are paid in SN25α to your Bittensor coldkey when you claim them."
msgstr "Os ganhos são liquidados a cada época e pagos em SN25α na sua coldkey Bittensor quando você os resgata."

#. Earnings card, after sn_payout_schedule: when the current epoch ends, when its share can be claimed and when an unclaimed share expires. The three values are local date-times the app fills from the chain's epoch schedule (the coordinator's policy: the claim-open offset and the claim TTL), never fixed durations.
msgctxt "sn_payout_schedule_times"
msgid "This epoch ends {0}. Claim your share from {1} until {2}."
msgstr "Esta época termina em {0}. Resgate sua parte de {1} até {2}."

#. Claim status of an epoch whose alpha can be claimed now.
msgctxt "sn_status_claimable"
msgid "Claimable"
msgstr "Resgatável"

#. Claim status of an epoch the SDK reports as not-finalized. Despite that name the vault has finalized the epoch: with no payout root (the root was missed, so no payout list was published for it and nothing can ever be claimed for it), or with a payout list that has no share for this wallet. Never 'Finalizing' or 'Not finalized', and no 'yet': nothing more is published for that epoch.
msgctxt "sn_status_not_finalized"
msgid "No payout published"
msgstr "Nenhum pagamento publicado"

#. Claim status of an epoch that is still open (not yet finalized on chain).
msgctxt "sn_status_open"
msgid "Open"
msgstr "Aberta"

#. Blockchain name. A product name: never translated.
msgctxt "solana"
msgid "Solana"
msgstr "Solana"

#. Note under the Solana payment button on the plan picker: Solana is a one-time yearly payment, the free trial is Stripe only.
msgctxt "solana_one_time_payment"
msgid "Paying with USDC on Solana is a one-time yearly payment, with no free trial."
msgstr "Pagar com USDC na Solana é um pagamento anual único, sem teste grátis."

#. Shown once when the check for a Solana Pay payment (started when the app returns from the wallet) has run 20 seconds without the payment landing. The check keeps going for up to two minutes; the app cannot know whether the wallet actually sent anything, so do not say the payment was received.
msgctxt "solana_payment_still_checking"
msgid "Still checking for your Solana payment. Confirmation on the network can take a minute or two."
msgstr "Ainda verificando seu pagamento Solana. A confirmação na rede pode levar um ou dois minutos."

#. Call to action
msgctxt "solana_sign_in"
msgid "Sign in with Solana"
msgstr "Entrar com Solana"

#. Label of the connected Solana wallet block on the Earnings screen (parallel to bittensor_wallet).
msgctxt "solana_wallet"
msgid "Solana wallet"
msgstr "Carteira Solana"

#. Error in the Solana payout wallet's connect sheet of the desktop apps (macOS, Windows, Linux) when the ur.io wallet bridge page returns extension_not_found: the chosen wallet's browser extension is not in this browser. The argument is the wallet product name (Phantom or Solflare). The sheet also takes a typed address, which works with any wallet, so the line points at its Enter address manually control, named in that control's own words (enter_address_manually). Signing in has no manual entry and keeps bittensor_error_extension_not_found.
msgctxt "solana_wallet_error_extension_not_found"
msgid "The {} extension was not found in this browser. Install it and try again, or choose “Enter address manually” to paste your wallet address."
msgstr "A extensão {} não foi encontrada neste navegador. Instale-a e tente novamente, ou escolha \"Digitar o endereço manualmente\" para colar o endereço da sua carteira."

#. Solana wallet error in the desktop apps (macOS, Windows, Linux) when the ur.io wallet bridge page returns session_not_found: the browser no longer has the wallet connection made in the connect step (another browser or a private window, or its site data was cleared), so nothing was signed. Starting again reconnects the wallet (Phantom or Solflare).
msgctxt "solana_wallet_error_session_not_found"
msgid "The wallet connection wasn't found in this browser. Start again to reconnect your wallet."
msgstr "A conexão da carteira não foi encontrada neste navegador. Comece de novo para reconectar sua carteira."

#. Used in Main/Account/Wallets/ConnectWalletSheet/ConnectWalletSheetView.swift.
msgctxt "solflare"
msgid "Solflare"
msgstr "Solflare"

#. Something went wrong error message
msgctxt "something_went_wrong"
msgid "Something went wrong."
msgstr "Algo deu errado."

#. Snackbar shown when the account lookup for a password reset fails. Used in Main/Account/Profile/ProfileView.swift.
msgctxt "something_went_wrong_finding_your_account"
msgid "Something went wrong finding your account"
msgstr "Algo deu errado ao localizar sua conta"

#. Used in Main/Account/Settings/UpdateReferralNetworkSheet/UpdateReferralNetworkSheetViewModel.swift.
msgctxt "something_went_wrong_please_try_again_later"
msgid "Something went wrong. Please try again later."
msgstr "Algo deu errado. Por favor, tente novamente mais tarde."

#. Call to action
msgctxt "sorry_to_see_you_go"
msgid "We're sorry to see you go!"
msgstr "Lamentamos ver você partir!"

#. A label displaying the number of split rules. The argument is the count of split rules.
msgctxt "split_rule_count"
msgid "{} split rule"
msgid_plural "{} split rules"
msgstr[0] "{} regra de divisão"
msgstr[1] "{} regras de divisão"

#. A description of the functionality of the split rule editor.
msgctxt "split_rule_description"
msgid "Selected hosts are routed locally and bypass the tunnel."
msgstr "Os hosts selecionados são roteados localmente e contornam o túnel."

#. Split rules: validation error for a host entry that is not a valid host name.
msgctxt "split_rule_error_bad_name"
msgid "Enter a host name like example.com."
msgstr "Insira um nome de host como example.com."

#. Split rules: validation error for an entry that looks like an IP range but is not a valid CIDR.
msgctxt "split_rule_error_bad_range"
msgid "Enter an IP range like 10.0.0.0/8."
msgstr "Insira um intervalo de IP como 10.0.0.0/8."

#. Split rules: validation error for a wildcard entry with nothing after the asterisk.
msgctxt "split_rule_error_bad_wildcard"
msgid "A wildcard needs a name after it, like *.example.com."
msgstr "Um curinga precisa de um nome depois dele, como *.example.com."

#. Split rules: validation error when a broader entry already in the rule covers the typed one. {rule} is that broader entry, for example *.example.com or 10.0.0.0/8.
msgctxt "split_rule_error_covered"
msgid "Already covered by {} in this rule."
msgstr "Já coberto por {} nesta regra."

#. Split rules: validation error when the typed entry is already in the rule.
msgctxt "split_rule_error_duplicate"
msgid "Already in this rule."
msgstr "Já está nesta regra."

#. Split rules: validation error for a host name with non-ASCII characters; the rule wants the punycode form.
msgctxt "split_rule_error_not_ascii"
msgid "Use the ASCII form of the name."
msgstr "Use a forma ASCII do nome."

#. Split rules: placeholder in the host input listing the accepted forms (a host name, a wildcard, a CIDR range).
msgctxt "split_rule_host_placeholder"
msgid "example.com, *.example.com, 10.0.0.0/8"
